{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/39997-the-mentor-background","id":39997,"title":"The Mentor Background","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-31T08:06:26-08:00","id":39997,"title":"The Mentor Background","content":"Have the Mentor-Background played a big role in your chronicles? In my chronicles it has been used quite a bit, especially if the PC:s have a good relation with their sires. Examples are a character from the Giovanni Chronicles who managed to get Hardestadt as a level 5-mentor and a Gangrel in Gary in the modern nights who had his sire Lucian as a level 3-mentor (an independent/autarkis-character embraced in the Roman-era).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1298-the-chronicler","name":"The Chronicler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T17:50:58-08:00","id":40264,"title":"","content":"It doesn't get used a lot in the games in my group. For a few reasons:<br /> 1) Most of the members of the group I'm in are those who've come together out of 3 other groups in the area that were left due to bad ST/DM/GM's, so some of us still have a few hang-ups about when and how to use character traits that are in the hands of the ST, especially when the points invested could be used in things like Generation, Retainers, Resources, Wonder, Totem, etc.<br /> 2) The players in the group who don't have those experiences are newer to the hobby, with the current group being their first foray into games other than D&amp;D, so they tend to follow suit with the rest of us in their CarGen habbits, for better and worse.<br /> 3) Many of the games we play kind of run with some form of the players starting out as being outcast or else separated from having a lot of support. Games as Orphans, games in Cam/Sab/Indy contested cities, games in newly set up caerns, etc. In these games, it would usually be difficult to explain and set up the Mentor.<br /> <br /> When Mentor does get used, it tends to be along with the Disembodied Mentor Merit (5-pt, Clanbook: Malkavian Rev.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>&quot;Maturity is knowing you were an idiot in the past.&quot;<br /> &quot;If that's true, then Wisdom is knowing you'll be an idiot in the future.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Common Sense is knowing that you should try not to be an idiot NOW.&quot;<br /> -Questionable Content 976</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1042-zhyzhaksmate","name":"ZhyzhaksMate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1042_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}